From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:56:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 458/488] [DS4.1] Run 19 fixes: column copies compile, host
 tests stub launches, bias restore

- columns.py: the row's address passes inline (bound to a variable it
  was declared void* from a const buffer, which nvcc refused), and the
  16-byte helpers take const destinations.
- Host tests of adaptive verification and DSpark's Markov drafter stub
  the TileLang row scatter and hidden-row gather they now reach; the rank
  declaration test counts the rank calls only.
- Logit bias: with an allowed list, the all-masked check reads back the
  allowed ids instead of rescanning the row (every other column is -inf
  or NaN after the fill). Run 19's gate had the min-tokens structured
  case at 96 rows 0.9% behind Triton; a new test covers biases meeting
  the fill.
